@startuml state-machine
' The incident lifecycle. One class per state in com.itsm.domain.state (State pattern).
title I-ITSM · Incident state machine

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F7F9FC
  BorderColor #4A5568
  ArrowColor #2D3748
}
hide empty description

[*] --> NEW : employee reports\nthe incident

NEW --> CLASSIFIED : system: priority calculated,\nSLA deadlines set
CLASSIFIED --> ASSIGNED : system: strategy chose a technician\nor administrator assigned one
ASSIGNED --> ACKNOWLEDGED : technician: "Acknowledge"\n/ response SLA met
ACKNOWLEDGED --> IN_PROGRESS : technician: "Start work"
IN_PROGRESS --> AWAITING_INFO : technician: "Request information"\n[note required] / SLA clock pauses
AWAITING_INFO --> IN_PROGRESS : employee: "Send information"\ntechnician: "Resume work"\n/ SLA clock resumes, deadline moves back
IN_PROGRESS --> RESOLVED : technician: "Resolve"\n[resolution note required]\n/ resolution SLA met or breached
RESOLVED --> VERIFIED : employee: "Confirm it is fixed"
RESOLVED --> IN_PROGRESS : employee: "Not fixed, reopen"\nadministrator: "Reopen" [note required]\n/ resolution forgotten, SLA clock resumes
VERIFIED --> CLOSED : technician or administrator: "Close"
CLOSED --> [*]

NEW : NewState
NEW : waiting for its priority
CLASSIFIED : ClassifiedState
CLASSIFIED : has a priority, waits for a technician
ASSIGNED : AssignedState
ASSIGNED : the response clock is running
ACKNOWLEDGED : AcknowledgedState
IN_PROGRESS : InProgressState
IN_PROGRESS : the resolution clock is running
AWAITING_INFO : AwaitingInfoState
AWAITING_INFO : SLA status PAUSED
RESOLVED : ResolvedState
RESOLVED : no longer counts as open
VERIFIED : VerifiedState
VERIFIED : can be rated
CLOSED : ClosedState
CLOSED : final: never changes again,\ncan still be rated

note right of CLASSIFIED
  If no technician can take it, the
  incident stays here and the
  administrators are warned.
end note

note as Rules
  **10 legal moves.** Any other move throws
  InvalidStateTransitionException and changes nothing.
  Reassigning (ASSIGNED … AWAITING_INFO) changes the
  technician but not the state.
end note
@enduml
